{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies an id reference."}],"metadata":{"title":"id","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV2idSSSgvp","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/id"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/id"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","title":"MXLMetronome","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLMetronome","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/id":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/id","title":"id","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is 